{
	"_doc": "Extra moves of bosses and crypt enemies (src/combat/boss_moves.gd, design docs/BOSS-FAEHIGKEITEN.de.md). Every move warns first (telegraph) and can be dodged. Times in seconds, distances in px, damage in half hearts (2 = one heart). sets: per enemy (key: 'void' for the Leerenrufer, else the enemy kind): every [min, max] seconds between moves (the enemy's own attacks run in between), rage_below: below this share of its HP the enemy rages once (roar, moves come faster by rage.cooldown_scale, 'rage' moves unlock), rebuild: the Knochenkoloss rises once (skull_share of max HP must be dealt to its skull within time, else it stands up with revive_share HP). A move entry: move id, weight, cooldown, near (only within px of the target), far (only beyond px), hp_below (share), once, rage (only while raging). moves: type is strikes (warning circles, pattern under_players / near_players / line / self / under_target), bullets (pattern single / fan / ring (with a gap) / spiral), lob (globs land after flight and leave a pool), dash (charge along a line; away: jump back), blink (teleport, pool left behind), vortex (pulls everyone in, then bursts), cone (breath in front), grab (seize and throw), spin (whirl around itself), summon (minions), armor (damage taken x scale for time, then shards), barrier (ice blocks to break), cage (blocks around a hero), shield (armor for the nearest ally), twin_beam (the Leerenrufer's beam as two beams with a safe gap). anim: attack, roar, summon or cast (the figure's clip). effect on hit: slow [speed share, seconds], poison [damage per second, seconds], freeze seconds, pull px. pool: style, radius, time, dps, slow, slip (ice: no grip).",
